            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Notes:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> The black tick is the simple average of hospitals in the same state with a result for that condition (each hospital counts equally), so in small states it may rest on only a few hospitals. Rows without a bar give CMS&apos;s reason: results not available for this period, too few cases to report, or no cases met the criteria. Hospitals are listed with city and state because some names repeat. 377 ratios nationwide use partial-period data under a CMS exception.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
