              <zone fixed-size='78' h='9556' id='13' is-fixed='true' mode='slider' param='[Parameters].[Parameter 0948661309857796]' type-v2='paramctrl' w='13417' x='85916' y='33444'>
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                </zone-style>
              </zone>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='12222' id='29' type-v2='text' w='98666' x='667' y='889'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='18'>Which hospitals readmit Medicare patients more often than expected?</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>CMS (Centers for Medicare &amp; Medicaid Services - Federal Agency) gives each hospital an excess readmission ratio for each condition: its 30-day readmissions compared with what it expects for similar patients at an average hospital. Above 1.0 = more readmissions than expected, below 1.0 = fewer. Titles describe all conditions combined; Use the Condition filter to find a particular condition.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555'>Source: CMS Hospital Readmissions Reduction Program, discharges July 2021 to June 2024. Medicare patients only.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='11000' id='32' type-v2='text' w='98666' x='667' y='88111'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Notes:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#555555' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
              <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Each hospital has up to six results, one per condition; shares count only results with a published ratio. </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Map:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'> states with fewer than 10 hospitals reporting a ratio are left blank (DC, DE, VT, ND, AK, WY and RI for all conditions; more for single conditions). </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Spread by condition</run>
              <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'> isn&apos;t affected by the Condition filter. </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Ownership:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'> Federal (13) and Tribal (5) hospitals are grouped as Other; groups with fewer than 10 hospitals are hidden. Minimum discharges = 0 includes every hospital; a higher value keeps only hospitals with published discharges at or above it, which also removes results where CMS hid the counts (fewer than 11 readmissions). </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'>Star rating:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#1b1b1b' fontsize='10'> 197 hospitals with a readmissions ratio have no rating and are left out. The star rating includes a readmission measure, so part of this link is built in. All charts show associations, not causes.</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
